## API (backend, optional)

- **`GET /health`** → `{ "ok": true }`
- **`POST /upload`** (`multipart/form-data`): `followersFile`, `followingFile` → `{ "non_followers": [...] }` (legacy Non-Followers; not exposed in current UI)

## Conventions

- Match existing style: focused diffs, no unrelated refactors.
- **Wrapped** (`/wrapped`) is client-only after export load: **ten 9:16 story cards** in a vertical scroller (scroll-snap, Prev/Next/dots/arrow keys, screenshot-friendly), light glass styling, per-slide accents (`wrappedThemes.js`), activity-style stack charts (`wrappedPalette.js`), body quips after charts, merged footer on data slides. Slide order: intro → span → activity → likes → comments → story interactions → DMs → profile searches → privacy → teaser. Orchestration: `wrappedData.js` (`loadWrappedBaseline`); reuses or fills `heatmapCache`, `socialGraphCache`, `messagesCache`.
- **Leaderboard slides:** [`WrappedAvatarPodium.jsx`](frontend/src/components/WrappedAvatarPodium.jsx) — initials circles in `.wrapped-podium__face` (clipped); rank badge `.wrapped-podium__badge` sits **outside** the circle. Leaderboard cards use `:has(.wrapped-leaderboard)` in CSS for extra padding and `overflow: visible` so badges are not clipped by the deck or card edges. Stack bar labels use `truncateLabel` in [`wrappedSlideContent.jsx`](frontend/src/pages/wrappedSlideContent.jsx) for on-screen fit only.
- When extending Instagram export parsing, reuse patterns from **`commentHeatmap.js`** and align with **`socialInteractionGraph.js`** where overlap exists.
- No new heavy chart libraries unless explicitly approved. Avoid re-adding **`html-to-image`** or similar for Save unless there is a dedicated export layout that does not depend on photographing the scroller card.

## Optional scoped rules

Add separate `.mdc` files with `globs` (e.g. `frontend/**/*.jsx`, `backend/**/*.js`) if you need frontend-only or backend-only guidance beyond this file.
